# UI

Light is locked. `color-scheme: only light`. Cool silver `--paper`, white `--surface`, ink CTAs. Do not add `prefers-color-scheme: dark`.

Outfit is the product face. Martian Mono is only for pairing codes, fingerprints, and the 12 words. Sheets use `--radius` and `--shadow`. Hover is `--wash`, not a full invert. Press uses `scale(0.98)`.

The signed-out home is an asymmetric split: headline left, demo sheet right. From 960px the clipboard is write left, tray right, one sheet. No hero glow, mesh, or beam.

First-run is one visible next action. The signed-out chrome is About, then Sign in, then Menu. The signed-out hero has one filled CTA. Guest Menu lists About and every onboarding path with a one-line hint — do not hide recover, pairing, or first-admin from a guest Menu. A signed-in working browser's Menu is the product, not disaster recovery: clipboard, both pairing roles, admin, Account, log out. Recover is only for a guest or a signed-in browser that has no keys yet. A guest without an invite is told they need a link. After a passkey, the 12 words are generated on that screen with a working label. Pairing is not a peer of invite redeem on the hero. `/pair` shows both pairing roles as cards and tags the likely one. Never hide a role or bounce a browser with a refusal — put the right screen one click away. Menu lists Show a code and Add a device when the account has keys. Forget is visible on every width. Invites are `/join?t=` URLs. Do not say “vault” on a screen a guest has to complete. ⌘K is not required to finish setup.

Never Inter. No emoji chrome. Composer Send / Ephemeral / File use the send, wifi, and folder marks on light chips, never on an ink fill. Notes may contain emoji and markdown; the composer suggestion list may show emoji. That is content, not chrome. Forget is a delete mark, Open is an expand mark, Copy is overlapping rectangles, Edit is a pencil mark, and Sync is a loading mark, all with accessible names, on the same row as the note and vertically centered with the text. The About questions open/close chip may use native platform emoji. Do not imply the server reads plaintext.
